 Tree Structure

        A
      /   \
     B     C
    / \     \
   D   E     F


 Root Node
- Definition: The root is the very first/top node of the tree, with no parent.  
A is the root node.

Leaf Nodes
- Definition: Leaf nodes are nodes with no children (endpoints of the tree).  
  - D (no children)  
  - E (no children)  
  - F (no children)  
- Leaf nodes = {D, E, F}

 Degree of Node B
- Definition: Degree of a node = number of children that node has.  
 Node B has two children (D and E).  
- Degree(B)= 2

 Height of Tree
- Definition: Height = longest path from root to a leaf (counting levels).  
- Path examples:  
  - A → B → D (3 levels)  
  - A → B → E (3 levels)  
  - A → C → F (3 levels)  
- Height = 3

 Level of Node E
- Definition: Level = distance from root, starting with root at level 1.  
  - Root A → Level 1  
  - Node B → Level 2  
  - Node E → Level 3  
-Level(E) = 3
